---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection, getEntry } from 'astro:content';

const projects = (await getCollection('projects')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
const visual = await getEntry('visual','visual');
const hero = visual.data.shots.filter(s=>s.category==='auto').slice(0,5);
---
<Base title="Thomas Chen — Information systems, design, video">

<section class="act" id="a0">
  <video id="reel" poster="/assets/poster.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata">
    <source src="/assets/reel-mobile.mp4" media="(max-width:700px)" type="video/mp4" />
    <source src="/assets/reel.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
  </video>
  <div class="veil"></div>
  <button class="vbtn m" id="rp">Pause</button>
  <div class="inner">
    <h1>Thomas<b>Chen.</b></h1>
    <div class="roles m">
      <span><i>✳</i>Information systems</span><span><i>✳</i>UX &amp; service design</span>
      <span><i>✳</i>Video &amp; photography</span><span><i>✳</i>Team PNG swimmer</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="act" id="a1"><div class="inner">
  <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>01</i> — Method</p>
  <h2 class="big rv">I take things apart.</h2>
  <p class="sub rv">Give me something that isn't working and I'll find where it actually breaks — not where it looks like it breaks. Here's a real one: a handwritten delivery slip from a distribution business in Port Moresby.</p>
  <div class="dissect">
    <div class="stage"><span class="cap">01 — As found</span><div class="in">
      <p class="scrawl">order #—<br />4 × tofu, 2 × noodle<br />K840 cash?<br />driver — <s>the usual guy</s><br />“left this morning”<br /><s>paid? ask later</s></p></div></div>
    <div class="stage"><span class="cap">02 — Taken apart</span><div class="in">
      <div class="field"><span>Customer</span><span>identified</span></div>
      <div class="field"><span>Items · value</span><span>K840.00</span></div>
      <div class="field"><span>Packed by</span><span class="miss">unrecorded</span></div>
      <div class="field"><span>Driver · vehicle</span><span class="miss">unlinked</span></div>
      <div class="field"><span>Delivered</span><span class="miss">unverified</span></div>
      <div class="field"><span>Cash returned</span><span class="miss">unreconciled</span></div>
    </div></div>
    <div class="stage"><span class="cap hi">03 — Put back</span><div class="in">
      <div class="lrow"><span class="tick">✓</span><span class="who">Packed · warehouse</span><span class="ts">08:12</span></div>
      <div class="lrow"><span class="tick">✓</span><span class="who">Assigned · dispatcher</span><span class="ts">08:40</span></div>
      <div class="lrow"><span class="tick">✓</span><span class="who">Delivered · proof captured</span><span class="ts">11:26</span></div>
      <div class="lrow"><span class="tick">✓</span><span class="who">Cash reconciled · office</span><span class="ts">16:03</span></div>
    </div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="verdict rv">The business thought it had a paperwork problem. It had an <b>accountability</b> problem — nothing tied an order to the person, vehicle and outcome behind it. Once that's the question, the answer stops being "an app" and becomes <b>an audit trail everything else has to serve</b>.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="act" id="a2"><div class="inner">
  <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>02</i> — Systems</p>
  <h2 class="big rv">Chain of custody.</h2>
  <p class="sub rv">Six stages, five roles, permissions enforced at the back end rather than hidden in the interface. The dashed stages are where the stock and the cash were actually going missing.</p>
  <div class="chain">
    <div class="node"><p class="st">Stage 01</p><p class="nm">Created</p><p class="rl">Office</p></div>
    <div class="node"><p class="st">Stage 02</p><p class="nm">Packed</p><p class="rl">Warehouse</p></div>
    <div class="node"><p class="st">Stage 03</p><p class="nm">Assigned</p><p class="rl">Dispatcher</p></div>
    <div class="node gap"><p class="st">Stage 04</p><p class="nm">In transit</p><p class="rl">Blind spot</p></div>
    <div class="node gap"><p class="st">Stage 05</p><p class="nm">Delivered</p><p class="rl">Unverified</p></div>
    <div class="node"><p class="st">Stage 06</p><p class="nm">Reconciled</p><p class="rl">Manager</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="verdict rv"><b>Delivery Control</b> — concept and systems design, 2026. Problem analysis, risk model, role and permission design, written specification. Not built.</p>
  <a class="go m rv" href="/projects/">See all {projects.length} projects →</a>
</div></section>

<section class="act" id="a3"><div class="inner">
  <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>03</i> — Structure</p>
  <h2 class="big rv">Twenty pages, one shape.</h2>
  <p class="sub rv">Toolbox Education was expanding from Victoria into New South Wales with a site that had grown by accretion. I restructured the information architecture and wired enquiry routing into their CRM pipelines.</p>
  <div class="ia">
    <div class="col"><p class="hd">Before — 20+ pages, flat</p>
      <span class="chip">Managing meltdowns</span><span class="chip">Book a call</span><span class="chip">NES</span>
      <span class="chip">Programs</span><span class="chip">About</span><span class="chip">NSW?</span>
      <span class="chip">Contact</span><span class="chip">Workshops</span><span class="chip">Schools</span>
      <span class="chip">Parents</span><span class="chip">Enquire</span><span class="chip">Resources</span></div>
    <div class="arrow">──→</div>
    <div class="col"><p class="hd">After — grouped by who's asking</p>
      <div class="tree"><p class="g">Programs/</p><p class="c">schools · parents · workshops</p>
      <p class="g">Regions/</p><p class="c">VIC · NSW</p>
      <p class="g">Enquire/</p><p class="c">book a call → HubSpot pipeline</p>
      <p class="g">About/</p><p class="c">team · approach · resources</p></div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="verdict rv">The pages weren't the problem. <b>Nobody could tell whether a page was for a parent or a principal</b> — so enquiries landed in the wrong place and got answered twice, or not at all.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="act" id="a4">
  <div class="slides" id="slides">
    {hero.map((s,i)=>(<div class={i===0?'slide on':'slide'}><img src={`/assets/${s.src}`} alt={s.title} loading={i===0?'eager':'lazy'} /></div>))}
  </div>
  <div class="veil"></div>
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>04</i> — Visual</p>
    <h2 class="big rv">And then there's the other half.</h2>
    <p class="sub rv">Thirty-plus commercial jobs since 2020 — automotive, brand, event and exhibition work. Directed, shot and cut end to end.</p>
    <div class="exif m" id="exif"></div>
    <a class="go m rv" href="/visual/">Open the full archive →</a>
  </div>
  <script is:inline define:vars={{hero}}>
    (function(){
      const sl=document.getElementById('slides'), ex=document.getElementById('exif');
      if(!sl||!hero.length) return;
      let i=0;
      const paint=()=>{const s=hero[i];ex.innerHTML=
        `<span>Frame <b>${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}/${String(hero.length).padStart(2,'0')}</b></span>`+
        `<span>Subject <b>${s.title}</b></span><span>Kit <b>${s.kit||'—'}</b></span><span>Year <b>${s.year||''}</b></span>`};
      paint();
      setInterval(()=>{sl.children[i].classList.remove('on');i=(i+1)%hero.length;
        sl.children[i].classList.add('on');paint()},3600);
    })();
  </script>
</section>

<section class="act" id="a5"><div class="inner">
  <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>05</i> — Who</p>
  <h2 class="big rv">Both halves, same person.</h2>
  <div class="who">
    <div>
      <p class="rv">I'm doing a <b>Master of Information Systems</b> at the University of Melbourne, after a design degree majoring in UX. In practice I'm as comfortable modelling roles and permissions as running a usability session.</p>
      <p class="rv">My family runs a vertically integrated food business in Port Moresby — the city's first tofu producer, three stores, a bakery and a delivery fleet. I've done operations and systems support there since 2022. That slip in Act 01 is real.</p>
      <p class="rv">I swim for <b>Papua New Guinea</b> — 50 breaststroke, butterfly, freestyle. World Championships, Pacific Games, Oceania Championships, and Short Course Worlds in Beijing this December. I got back after labrum surgery and an ACL reconstruction. Two years. It taught me more about following a plan than any job has.</p>
      <p class="rv">Away from a screen I <b>work on cars and fix machinery</b>. Same instinct as everything above: take it apart, find where it's actually failing, put it back properly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card rv">
      <img src="/assets/me-personal.webp" alt="Thomas Chen" />
      <div class="li"><s>Based</s><em>Melbourne, VIC</em></div>
      <div class="li"><s>Studying</s><em>M. Information Systems</em></div>
      <div class="li"><s>Languages</s><em>EN · 中文 · Tok Pisin</em></div>
      <div class="li"><s>Swimming</s><em>Team PNG, 2023–</em></div>
      <div class="li"><s>Next meet</s><em>SC Worlds, Beijing</em></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="act" id="a6"><div class="inner">
  <p class="actno m rv">Act <i>06</i> — Contact</p>
  <h2 class="big rv">Tell me what's<br />not working.</h2>
  <p class="sub rv" style="margin:18px auto 0">Hiring for systems, BA or product? Need video or photography? Fifteen minutes is usually enough to know if it's a fit.</p>
  <div class="cbtns rv">
    <a class="pri" href="https://cal.com/thomas-chen">Book a call →</a>
    <a href="mailto:thomasjiahao@gmail.com">Email</a>
    <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/thomas-j-chen">LinkedIn</a>
  </div>
  <p class="m dim rv" style="margin-top:30px">Usually replies within a day · Melbourne, AEST</p>
</div></section>

<script is:inline>
  const names={a0:'00 — Intro',a1:'01 — Method',a2:'02 — Systems',a3:'03 — Structure',a4:'04 — Visual',a5:'05 — Who',a6:'06 — Contact'};
  const io=new IntersectionObserver(es=>es.forEach(e=>{
    if(e.isIntersecting){e.target.classList.add('seen');
      if(e.intersectionRatio>.5){const f=document.getElementById('f-sec');if(f)f.textContent=names[e.target.id]||''}}
  }),{threshold:[.15,.55]});
  document.querySelectorAll('.act').forEach(a=>io.observe(a));
  const vid=document.getElementById('reel'), rp=document.getElementById('rp');
  if(vid&&rp) rp.onclick=()=>{if(vid.paused){vid.play();rp.textContent='Pause'}else{vid.pause();rp.textContent='Play'}};
</script>
</Base>
